<title>SWEDEN: Kinnevik posts 62 pct fall in Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>Kinnevik posts 62 pct fall in Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish media and investment group Kinnevik on Tuesday released these earnings for the three months ending on March 31, 1997. All comparison figures for the first quarter of 1996 are pro forma.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		   159  vs   423</p>
<p> Sales					1,821  vs 1,775</p>
<p> Shr (crowns)				2.50  vs  7.46</p>
<p> Costs of goods and services sold   1,431  vs 1,335</p>
<p> Other costs				  268  vs   250</p>
<p> Income from company development	 22  vs   333</p>
<p> Capital gain on selling securities   165  vs   nil</p>
<p> Other operating income		    76  vs    28</p>
<p> Other operating costs		     94  vs    88</p>
<p> Operating profit			   291  vs   463</p>
<p> Interests in associates	 CHARGE  51  vs    17 CHARGE</p>
<p> Net financial items	     CHARGE  81  vs    23 CHARGE</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			     157  vs   517</p>
<p> Minorities				     3  vs     7</p>
<p>NOTE -- The full company name is Industriforvaltnings AB Kinnevik.</p>
<p>All the figures, for both quarters, exclude NetCom Systems AB and the Modern Times Group MTG AB, which the company has spun off.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
